# Dart Code Style – AskmeHUMG

## General Rules
- Follow `flutter_lints` and `analysis_options.yaml`
- Prefer `final` over `var` whenever the value is not reassigned
- Use `const` constructors for widgets that don't change
- Never suppress analyzer warnings with `// ignore:` unless truly unavoidable

## Null Safety
```dart
// ✅ GOOD
final email = user.email ?? '';
final name = user.displayName ?? 'Anonymous';
```

## Async / Future
```dart
// ✅ Always await, always handle error
try {
  await someFirebaseCall();
} on FirebaseException catch (e, s) {
  logger.e('Firebase error', error: e, stackTrace: s);
  throw SomeFailure(e.message ?? 'error');
}
```

## Widget Best Practices
```dart
// ✅ Extract sub-widgets, use const
class QuestionCard extends StatelessWidget {
  const QuestionCard({super.key, required this.question});
  final Question question;
}
```

## Riverpod
- One feature = one `<feature>_providers.dart` file
- Co-locate providers with the feature: `lib/app/modules/feed/presentation/feed_providers.dart`
- `ref.watch` in `build()`, `ref.read` in callbacks/handlers

## Localization
- All user-facing strings: `AppLocalizations.of(context).*`
- Never hardcode display strings in widget code
- ARB files: `lib/l10n/app_vi.arb`, `app_en.arb`, `app_ja.arb`

## Logging
```dart
import 'package:askme_humg/app/core/utils/logger.dart';

logger.d('debug message');
logger.i('info');
logger.w('warning');
logger.e('error occurred', error: e, stackTrace: s);
```
Never use `print()`.

## Icons — always use LucideIcons
```dart
// ✅ Use lucide_icons_flutter
import 'package:lucide_icons_flutter/lucide_icons.dart';

Icon(LucideIcons.circleAlert)   // error
Icon(LucideIcons.inbox)         // empty state
Icon(LucideIcons.lock)          // anonymous/locked
Icon(LucideIcons.chevronRight)  // navigation cue
Icon(LucideIcons.circleX)       // dismiss/error action

// ❌ Never use Material Icons
// Icons.error_outline_rounded
// Icons.inbox_outlined
```

## Type-safe assets
```dart
// ✅ Use flutter_gen generated accessors
Assets.imagesAppIcon.image(width: 180, height: 180)
Assets.svgsGoogleLogo.svg(width: 20, height: 20)

// ❌ Never hardcode asset paths
// 'assets/images/app_icon.png'
// Image.asset('assets/...')
```

## Import Order (enforced by dart format)
1. `dart:` packages
2. `package:flutter/`
3. Third-party packages
4. Internal `package:askme_humg/` imports
